One correction before we call Day 10 finished

Our current suspicious-port rule is a basic heuristic, not an AI model and not proof of an attack.

That's intentional.

The next improvement should be to combine multiple signals rather than declaring an attack from a port alone:

Suspicious port
      +
Unexpected process
      +
External destination
      +
Repeated connections
      +
Abnormal behavior
      ↓
Risk score
      ↓
Decision

That will make ACTDRS substantially more defensible as a cybersecurity project.

